cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this Lean formalization, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "elliptic-schauder-theory: Hölder spaces and flat-boundary Schauder theory in Lean"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/willmfeldman/elliptic-schauder-theory"
authors:
  - family-names: Feldman
    given-names: "William M."
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of linear elliptic Schauder theory: Hölder spaces on sets and
  Campanato's characterization; interior and flat-boundary C^{1,α} and C^{2,α} regularity in
  divergence form (L² Campanato on the gradient field, conormal boundary condition) and in
  nondivergence form (sup-norm Campanato, conormal-compatible and Dirichlet boundary
  conditions); and C^{k+1} regularity up to the flat boundary and scaled estimates for the
  quasilinear conormal problem div Φ(∇w) = 0.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formalized mathematics
  - elliptic partial differential equations
  - Schauder estimates
  - Campanato spaces
  - Hölder spaces
